# Mem0 auto-write (mandatory)

When **AutoLinkingBrain** MCP is available, persist knowledge **in the same session** you learn it.

## When to call storeKnowledge

| Trigger | scenario | Example |
|---------|----------|---------|
| Chose architecture / pattern | architecture | "Auth uses JWT in middleware X" |
| Fixed non-trivial bug | bugfix | root cause + fix location |
| Changed or added API | api_contract | endpoint, DTO, breaking change |
| Completed reindex slice | indexing | module map, entrypoints |
| Learned project-specific gotcha | architecture | env, deploy, config trap |

One fact per call. Include a **file path** in `text` or pass `context_path`.

## Minimum per session

- **Start:** `checkProjectHealth` (or `sessionContextPack` once).
- **During:** ≥1 `storeKnowledge` if you made any decision or discovery worth recalling.
- **End of task:** if nothing stored yet but work was done → one summary `storeKnowledge`.

## MCP call pattern

```
server: user-AutoLinkingBrain
tool: storeKnowledge
{ text: "English fact with path src/foo.py ...", tech: "...", scenario: "architecture", scope: "project", context_path: "..." }
```

If MCP errors: note briefly, continue work — retry store on next stable turn.
